  "findings": [
    "Both captures prove the Apple M4 Pro Metal target, exact-output correctness completion, profile-region markers, the declared trailing warmup/profile dispatch counts, and counter samples spanning more than 99.8% of each profile window.",
    "No target compiler-spill event and zero sampled threadgroup-memory L1 read/write bandwidth appeared in either capture. Those are capture-bounded observations, not universal absence claims.",
    "The Q window had a 31.06% median Instruction Throughput Limiter, 12.76% MMU Limiter, and 14.30% Last Level Cache Limiter. The rotating window had 5.91%, 25.92%, and 31.95%, respectively.",
    "The differing limiter mix is consistent with the rotating-weight workload exercising a different memory-system envelope, but these are single, device-wide captures with different GPU performance-state distributions. They do not establish a cache or bandwidth cause.",
    "Instrumented intervals are diagnostic and are not substituted for the ordinary AC timing baseline."
  ],
  "decision": "Close the baseline characterization without changing production dispatch. The two-output candidate failed its preregistered timing rule and therefore remains unprofiled; no candidate mechanism or M/N selector is inferred from these baseline-only traces."
